<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Early Lê dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">980–<a href="/years/1009">1009</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Early Le dynasty, Former Lê dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Early Lê dynasty ruled Đại Cồ Việt, in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, from 980 to 1009. Its founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-dai-hanh">Lê Hoàn</a> took power from the Đinh dynasty as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> invasion loomed and defeated the Song in 981, also campaigning against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/champa">Champa</a>. After the violent reign of his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-long-dinh">Lê Long Đĩnh</a>, the court chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ly-thai-to">Lý Công Uẩn</a>, who founded the Lý dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/early-le-dynasty.jpg" alt="Early Lê dynasty" width="320" height="345" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Night Lantern · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vietnam_(1009-1225).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The dynasty is called 'Later' to distinguish it from the <b>Early Lê</b> of 980–1009.</blockquote><a href="/empire/later-le-dynasty">Later Le dynasty · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
